WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.257
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:09.025
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:16.319
Unit five: Gerunds & Infinitives. Today you will choose between -ing and to + verb after other verbs.

4
00:00:16.619 --> 00:00:19.272
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:23.373
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.217 --> 00:00:24.939
Doing.

7
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.182
Doing means the -ing form used as a noun.

8
00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:30.202
Swimming is fun.

9
00:00:30.817 --> 00:00:33.121
Your turn. Say: Doing.

10
00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:36.654
Doing.

11
00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:38.267
To do.

12
00:00:39.283 --> 00:00:41.236
To do means to + base verb.

13
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.107
I want to swim.

14
00:00:43.717 --> 00:00:46.114
Your turn. Say: To do.

15
00:00:48.967 --> 00:00:49.782
To do.

16
00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:51.715
Enjoy doing.

17
00:00:52.717 --> 00:00:55.436
Enjoy doing means a verb followed by a gerund.

18
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.272
I enjoy reading.

19
00:00:57.883 --> 00:01:00.861
Your turn. Say: Enjoy doing.

20
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:04.922
Enjoy doing.

21
00:01:05.683 --> 00:01:06.592
Want to do.

22
00:01:07.583 --> 00:01:10.303
Want to do means a verb followed by an infinitive.

23
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:12.080
I want to learn.

24
00:01:12.683 --> 00:01:15.011
Your turn. Say: Want to do.

25
00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:18.717
Want to do.

26
00:01:19.483 --> 00:01:20.368
Gerund.

27
00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:23.743
Gerund means a verb used as a noun.

28
00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.850
Reading is a gerund.

29
00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:29.079
Your turn. Say: Gerund.

30
00:01:31.933 --> 00:01:32.737
Gerund.

31
00:01:33.483 --> 00:01:34.577
Infinitive.

32
00:01:35.583 --> 00:01:38.129
Infinitive means to + base verb.

33
00:01:38.717 --> 00:01:40.333
To read is an infinitive.

34
00:01:40.917 --> 00:01:43.476
Your turn. Say: Infinitive.

35
00:01:46.333 --> 00:01:47.474
Infinitive.

36
00:01:48.217 --> 00:01:49.322
Verb pattern.

37
00:01:50.317 --> 00:01:53.257
Verb pattern means the usual grammar after a verb.

38
00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.513
Learn each verb pattern.

39
00:01:56.117 --> 00:01:58.932
Your turn. Say: Verb pattern.

40
00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:02.721
Verb pattern.

41
00:02:03.483 --> 00:02:04.763
Depends on verb.

42
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:08.969
Depends on verb means the choice depends on the main verb.

43
00:02:09.583 --> 00:02:11.118
It depends on the verb.

44
00:02:11.717 --> 00:02:15.147
Your turn. Say: Depends on verb.

45
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.373
Depends on verb.

46
00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:23.922
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.783 --> 00:02:28.281
Visal, which do you prefer: enjoy doing or want to do?

48
00:02:29.383 --> 00:02:38.064
Both are correct, but with different verbs. I enjoy reading, but I want to learn Japanese. The choice depends on the main verb.

49
00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.929
Which verbs take the gerund?

50
00:02:42.017 --> 00:02:56.537
Enjoy, avoid, finish, suggest, consider, mind, keep and admit take -ing. We also use -ing after prepositions: She is good at drawing. And as a subject: Learning takes time.

51
00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.324
Which take the infinitive?

52
00:03:00.417 --> 00:03:16.481
Want, decide, hope, plan, manage, refuse and afford take to + verb. A few, like like, love, start and begin, take both with little change. Others, like stop and remember, change meaning.

53
00:03:17.633 --> 00:03:19.331
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:20.183 --> 00:03:24.609
Grammar focus: Verb patterns: gerund vs infinitive.

55
00:03:24.909 --> 00:03:26.177
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:26.883 --> 00:03:28.674
I enjoy reading in the evening.

57
00:03:29.583 --> 00:03:31.316
I want to learn Japanese.

58
00:03:32.217 --> 00:03:33.601
She is good at drawing.

59
00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:44.164
Enjoy, avoid, finish, suggest, consider + -ing. Want, decide, hope, plan, manage, refuse + to-infinitive. After prepositions use -ing.

60
00:03:44.917 --> 00:03:48.254
Be careful! Don't say: He suggested to go home.

61
00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.699
Say: He suggested going home.

62
00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:54.720
Suggest takes the gerund.

63
00:03:55.533 --> 00:03:58.313
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.240
-ing or To?.

65
00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.540
I enjoy reading in the evening.

66
00:04:03.533 --> 00:04:05.974
I also want to learn Japanese next year.

67
00:04:06.967 --> 00:04:10.348
She decided to move abroad, and he suggested going together.

68
00:04:11.333 --> 00:04:15.574
After a preposition, we always use the gerund, as in 'interested in learning'.

69
00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:19.449
Each verb pattern must be learned with practice.

70
00:04:20.533 --> 00:04:24.535
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:25.383 --> 00:04:26.872
I avoid blank late.

72
00:04:27.172 --> 00:04:30.918
A, to stay. B, staying. C, stay.

73
00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:36.582
The answer is B: staying.

74
00:04:37.717 --> 00:04:39.380
They decided blank early.

75
00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.985
A, to leave. B, leaving. C, leave.

76
00:04:46.533 --> 00:04:48.289
The answer is A: to leave.

77
00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.426
She is interested blank painting.

78
00:04:51.726 --> 00:04:54.463
A, in. B, to. C, at.

79
00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.465
The answer is A: in.

80
00:05:00.617 --> 00:05:01.943
Which is correct?

81
00:05:02.243 --> 00:05:07.684
A, He suggested to go.. B, He suggested going.. C, He suggested go..

82
00:05:11.233 --> 00:05:13.767
The answer is B: He suggested going..

83
00:05:14.917 --> 00:05:17.880
According to the reading, what does the writer want to learn?

84
00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:21.357
A, Japanese. B, French. C, music.

85
00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.760
The answer is A: Japanese.

86
00:05:27.967 --> 00:05:31.304
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:35.949
Use both a gerund and an infinitive in two separate sentences.

88
00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:46.169
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:46.469 --> 00:05:59.271
I enjoy learning languages, and I plan to study Spanish next year. I avoid speaking too fast, and I hope to improve my pronunciation. I choose -ing or to depending on the main verb.

90
00:05:59.571 --> 00:06:01.269
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:02.183 --> 00:06:07.866
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and verb patterns: gerund vs infinitive.

92
00:06:08.166 --> 00:06:12.153
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

93
00:06:12.453 --> 00:06:15.094
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

94
00:06:15.394 --> 00:06:18.848
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

